            "orig_filename": "710641__lonerdroner__preparing-breakfast.wav",
            "link": "https://freesound.org/people/lonerdroner/sounds/710641/",
            "author": "lonerdroner",
            "title": "preparing breakfast",
            "description": "Recorded with a Roland R-07 placed about a foot above the worktop and about five feet away to the right of an electric cooker to avoid any splashes from the eggs fried in lard. I boiled the water for coffee on a little gas camping stove (can’t really hear it), I prefer this as you get a nice creamy froth when you sprinkle on your coffee and it just tastes better than pouring boiled kettle water into the pot on top of the coffee. Two eggs (frying towards the end). A slice of bread and a clove of raw garlic. I sneezed once (edited out) a few sighs here and there remain. Salt and pepper mill sounds at the end and off I go.\n\nWindshield is on the recorder just to protect it from condensation. Input level 60, amplified by 5dB. No other processing.",
